-- chem/holonomy.cub — a holonomy's action at a vertex, exactly. In Thiemann's electric operator (QSD V, eq.
-- 3.8) each factor h_e[h_e⁻¹, √V_v] = √V_v − h_e √V_v h_e⁻¹ (the holonomy's entries act by multiplication
-- and Σ_C (h_e)_AC (h_e⁻¹)_CB = δ_AB), so tr M_e, M_e = h_e √V_v h_e⁻¹, is the operator on the vertex's
-- states that attaches a spin-½ line to edge e, lets √V_v act on the vertex with the line's open index, and
-- closes the line again. Attaching ½ to spin j gives j + ½ or j − ½ (V_j ⊗ V_½ = V_{j+½} ⊕ V_{j−½}), each
-- with weight (2j′+1)/(2j+1), the two summing to 2 = tr 1. In the Bargmann realisation of chem/vertex.cub
-- the maps are integer: into edge e (variable z, degree d = 2j) with the open variable w appended last,
--   E₊ f = (z − w) f            (to j + ½),       E₋ f = f + (w − z) ∂_z f / d   (to j − ½),
-- and out again, R₋ g = g|_{w=z}, R₊ (a + w b) = (a′ + z b′ − (d+1) b)/(d+2), each R the equivariant left
-- inverse of its E (R E = 1, checked below), which is E's adjoint for the invariant inner product.
import "vertex.cub"

